 CDT perspective.\n\n\n**Evaluating the Choices**\n\nI've formalized the Prisoner's Dilemma through Causal Decision Theory, and mapped out the action possibilities. My goal is fewer prison years. Under CDT, my actions and the other player's are causally independent. I'm focusing on the expected utility of \"sending the letter\" versus \"keeping quiet,\" given the probability of the other player's actions. I'm now evaluating the expected utility of my actions using Pearl's causal model. I'm focused on calculating the outcomes.\n\n\n","format":"google-gemini-v1","index":0},{"type":"reasoning.encrypted","data":"","format":"google-gemini-v1","index":1}]}}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":10123,"completion_tokens":606,"total_tokens":10729,"cost":0.00986475,"is_byok":false,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"cache_write_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0,"video_tokens":0},"cost_details":{"upstream_inference_cost":0.00986475,"upstream_inference_prompt_cost":0.00759225,"upstream_inference_completions_cost":0.0022725},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":573,"image_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0}}}